    'incident.s5.body' => "The reasoning is Mosca's inequality (2015) read backwards: the adversary is not waiting any more, they hold the data, and the only question is how much of the confidentiality asked for the cryptography can still deliver.",
    'incident.s5.formula' => 'year taken + declared confidentiality lifetime > algorithm expiry ⟹ the difference is the part that becomes readable',
    'incident.s5.declared' => 'The domains treated here are the ones somebody declared breached. A stolen table is not a statement about the whole system, and the tool declares none by itself.',
